  "body": "CONJUNCTIONAL INCENTIVE - A conjunctional bonus is being offered to any introducing/selling agent , please contact Jayden for full incentive details.\r\n\r\nDiscover a home that offers more than just a place to live. Perfectly positioned opposite Pigeon Mountain Reserve, this 601sqm (more or less) freehold property combines space, privacy, modern energy efficiency and exciting future potential - a rare find in Half Moon Bay.\r\n\r\nRecently refreshed and move-in ready, the home features fresh exterior and garage paint, brand-new carpet, a rebuilt deck and professionally landscaped gardens. Everything has been professionally cleaned, leaving you free to simply move in and enjoy.\r\n\r\nSecurity, parking and practicality are well catered for. An electric gate, keypad entry, video intercom, safety beams and battery backup provide peace of mind. The generous driveway accommodates multiple vehicles, a boat or campervan, while the impressive 5.1m x 10m garage offers excellent space for a workshop, home gym or storage.\r\n\r\nEnjoy the benefits of modern energy efficiency. Eighteen German-made Harrison solar panels, paired with a Tesla Powerwall 3 and 10kW inverter, generate approximately 30-50kWh on most days to help power the home, heat pumps and garden lighting. An external 16-amp socket with charging adaptor is also ready for your EV.\r\n\r\nInside, character meets quality. The distinctive Rimu kitchen features stone benchtops, handmade Middle Earth tiles, a Belling 900 induction range with double ovens, a plumbed Samsung fridge and LED-lit pantry shelving. Terracotta floors, a cosy log burner, new insulation and quality Harrisons carpet add warmth and comfort.\r\n\r\nAccommodation includes three generous bedrooms plus a separate 10sqm insulated sleeper cabin with its own heat pump - ideal as a home office, teenage retreat, guest space or potential Airbnb accommodation (subject to applicable approvals).\r\n\r\nThe private rear garden features mature fruit trees, including avocado trees nearly ready for harvest, with room for a spa or outdoor retreat. A rear gate also provides convenient access to Darren Park playground.\r\n\r\nLocation is another standout. Opposite the upgraded Pigeon Mountain Reserve and close to Highland Park Shopping Centre, local schools and Half Moon Bay Marina, you'll enjoy easy access to cafés, ferry services and coastal walks.\r\n\r\nWhether you're a family seeking space and security, an investor looking for a versatile freehold property, or a developer exploring future possibilities (subject to Council approval and applicable regulations), this property offers plenty to consider.\r\n\r\nSpace, privacy, solar efficiency and future potential - discover a different standard of Half Moon Bay living!",
